+             * same value every time, so comparing it with the ~0 recorded at the previous
+             * acquisition said "untouched" -- the opposite of what it means. MEASURED (Premiere
+             * 2026, 2026-10-16): the timeline ruler's bitmap answered ~0 for its whole life (an
+             * uninitialized lock count in windowscodecs, fixed there too), 209 of 210 acquisitions
+             * skipped the seed on ~0 == ~0 and published a stale copy, and old ruler numbers piled
